      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="badge badge-get">GET</span><br><code>/admin/staff/:id</code></td>
        <td><code>id</code> (UUID v4 via <code>ParseUUIDPipe</code>)</td>
        <td>Retrieves staff profile by ID. Throws <code>404 Not Found</code> if user does not exist or has customer role.</td>
        <td>None (Read-only query).</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="badge badge-patch">PATCH</span><br><code>/admin/staff/:id</code></td>
        <td><code>UpdateStaffDto</code>:<br><code>fullName?</code>, <code>role?</code>, <code>status?</code></td>
        <td>Loads existing user to capture <code>before</code> state. Applies partial updates in an atomic transaction.</td>
        <td><code>STAFF_UPDATED</code> with exact <code>before</code> and <code>after</code> state diffs.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="badge badge-delete">DELETE</span><br><code>/admin/staff/:id</code></td>
        <td><code>id</code> (UUID v4 via <code>ParseUUIDPipe</code>)</td>
        <td>Soft-deletes the staff member by setting <code>status = INACTIVE</code>. Immediately revokes JWT access.</td>
        <td><code>STAFF_DEACTIVATED</code> with <code>before</code> and <code>after</code> state.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <hr>

  <h2>5. Multi-Table Atomic Database Transactions</h2>
  <div class="callout">
    <div class="callout-title">Core Grading Requirement M2 & Course Bonus</div>
    <p>Every modifying administrative operation (staff creation, profile updates, and deactivations) executes inside an atomic PostgreSQL transaction using TypeORM's <code>DataSource.transaction()</code>. The user record mutation and the corresponding security audit log are bound together atomically.</p>
  </div>

  <h3>Transaction Implementation Walkthrough (<code>src/modules/users/users.service.ts</code>):</h3>
  <pre>async createStaff(actorId: string, input: CreateStaffDto): Promise&lt;SafeUser&gt; {
  const email = input.email.toLowerCase().trim();
  const existing = await this.users.findOne({ where: { email } });
  if (existing) {
    throw new ConflictException('Email already registered');
  }

  const passwordHash = await hash(input.password, 12);

  // START ATOMIC DATABASE TRANSACTION
  return this.dataSource.transaction(async (manager) => {
    const userRepository = manager.getRepository(User);
    
    // 1. Create and save the new staff user
    const user = await userRepository.save(
      userRepository.create({
        email,
        fullName: input.fullName.trim(),
        passwordHash,
        role: input.role,
        status: UserStatus.ACTIVE,
      }),
    );

    // 2. Write immutable audit log within the SAME transaction manager
    await this.audit.record(
      {
        actorId,
        action: 'STAFF_CREATED',
        entity: 'users',
        entityId: user.id,
        after: {
          email: user.email,
          fullName: user.fullName,
          role: user.role,
          status: user.status,
        },
      },
      manager, // Passes the transactional EntityManager!
    );

    // 3. Return sanitized user
    return {
      id: user.id,
      email: user.email,
      fullName: user.fullName,
      role: user.role,
      status: user.status,
      createdAt: user.createdAt,
      updatedAt: user.updatedAt,
    };
  }); // TRANSACTION COMMITS AUTOMATICALLY IF NO ERRORS THROWN
}</pre>

  <p><strong>Atomicity Guarantee:</strong> If the audit log insertion fails (e.g., due to a disk failure, database constraint, or connection glitch), the transaction automatically aborts (<code>ROLLBACK</code>), ensuring that an un-audited user is never committed to the database.</p>

  <hr>

  <h2>6. System Audit Trail & Logging (<code>audit</code>)</h2>

  <h3>6.1 Database Schema & Migration</h3>
  <p>Authored migration <code>1794470400010-CreateAuditLogs.ts</code> creating the <code>audit_logs</code> table:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>id</code>: UUID Primary Key (default <code>gen_random_uuid()</code>).</li>
    <li><code>actor_id</code>: Foreign Key referencing <code>users(id) ON DELETE SET NULL</code> (preserves audit records even if an actor is removed).</li>
    <li><code>action</code>: <code>VARCHAR(64)</code> (e.g., <code>STAFF_CREATED</code>, <code>STAFF_UPDATED</code>, <code>STAFF_DEACTIVATED</code>).</li>
    <li><code>entity</code>: <code>VARCHAR(64)</code> (target table, e.g., <code>users</code>).</li>
    <li><code>entity_id</code>: <code>VARCHAR(64)</code> (UUID of modified entity).</li>
    <li><code>before</code>: <code>JSONB</code> nullable (snapshot of entity state before modification).</li>
    <li><code>after</code>: <code>JSONB</code> nullable (snapshot of entity state after modification).</li>
    <li><code>created_at</code>: <code>TIMESTAMPTZ</code> UTC timestamp (indexed for range queries).</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>6.2 Browsing Audit Logs (<code>GET /api/v1/admin/audit-logs</code>)</h3>
  <p>Administrators can inspect system events using <code>AuditController</code> with comprehensive filtering:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Filter by <code>action</code> (e.g. <code>?action=STAFF_DEACTIVATED</code>).</li>
    <li>Filter by <code>entity</code> (e.g. <code>?entity=users</code>).</li>
    <li>Filter by <code>actorId</code> (to view all actions taken by a specific administrator).</li>
    <li>1-based pagination with <code>page</code> and <code>limit</code>.</li>
    <li>Returns actor relationship: includes actor's email, full name, and role for clear accountability.</li>
  </ul>

  <hr>

  <h2>7. Platform Analytics & Reporting (<code>analytics</code>)</h2>
  <p>Admin endpoint <code>GET /api/v1/admin/analytics/summary</code> aggregates critical business and operational statistics across the platform in real time using PostgreSQL native aggregation:</p>

  <h3>7.1 Real-Time PostgreSQL Queries Executed</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>User Census by Role & Status:</strong>
      <pre>SELECT "role", "status", COUNT(*)::int AS "count"
FROM "users"
GROUP BY "role", "status";</pre>
      Groups counts into active/inactive breakdowns and role totals (customer, staff, inventoryManager, admin).
    </li>
    <li><strong>Audit Volume & 24-Hour Velocity:</strong>
      <pre>SELECT COUNT(*)::int AS "count" FROM "audit_logs";
SELECT COUNT(*)::int AS "count" FROM "audit_logs"
WHERE "created_at" >= NOW() - INTERVAL '24 hours';</pre>
      Measures total audit volume and recent administrative velocity over the past 24 hours.
    </li>
    <li><strong>System Catalog & Order Counts:</strong>
      <pre>SELECT COUNT(*)::int AS "count" FROM "orders";
SELECT COUNT(*)::int AS "count" FROM "products";</pre>
      Provides total volume of commercial orders placed and products cataloged.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h3>7.2 Analytics Response Shape</h3>
  <pre>{
  "success": true,
  "message": "OK",
  "data": {
    "users": {
      "total": 6,
      "active": 5,
      "inactive": 1,
      "byRole": {
        "customer": 2,
        "staff": 2,
        "inventoryManager": 1,
        "admin": 1
      }
    },
    "audit": {
      "totalLogs": 12,
      "recentActionsCount": 4
    },
    "system": {
      "ordersCount": 3,
      "productsCount": 4
    }
  },
  "meta": {
    "requestId": "6f2d7ea0-6df8-41f5-a28a-493bdaed806d"
  }
}</pre>

  <hr>

  <h2>8. Request Validation & Controlled Exception Handling</h2>

  <h3>8.1 DTO Validation</h3>
  <p>THREAD enforces global validation using <code>ValidationPipe</code> with strict options:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>whitelist: true</code>: Automatically strips any property not defined in the DTO class.</li>
    <li><code>forbidNonWhitelisted: true</code>: Rejects the request with <code>400 Bad Request</code> if unexpected fields are provided.</li>
    <li><code>transform: true</code>: Automatically transforms primitive strings into numbers/booleans where annotated.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>8.2 Global HttpExceptionFilter</h3>
  <p>Located in <code>src/common/filters/http-exception.filter.ts</code>, this filter guarantees consistent error responses across all modules:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Catches PostgreSQL unique constraint violation error code <code>23505</code> and converts it into a client-safe <code>409 Conflict</code> (e.g. "Email already registered").</li>
    <li>Catches validation errors and formats them into a clean <code>details</code> array specifying the field and validation issue.</li>
    <li>Hides database connection strings, SQL queries, and stack traces from leaking to the client in production.</li>
  </ul>

  <hr>

